INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT #1#

Wind howls against the glass. MARA (40s), keeper of the light, winds the lamp's clockwork by hand. This line is long enough to wrap onto a second line in any template.

She checks the log book: *italic*, **bold**, _underlined_, and ***bold italic***.

MARA (V.O.)
Forty years of storms, and not one ship lost.
(beat)
Not one.

MARA
Who's there?

VOICE (O.S.) ^
Only the tide.

.CLOSE ON THE LAMP

It flickers.

CUT TO:

EXT. ROCKS BELOW - CONTINUOUS #2#

A small boat, empty, knocks against the stones.

~The sea gives, the sea takes,
~And the keeper keeps the light.

